%% Figure 10 — User Administration Access Lifecycle
flowchart LR
  Admin([Active PM with UserAdmin]) --> UI[User Administration workspace]
  UI --> Auth{CAP confirms exactly one PM role\nand UserAdmin capability?}
  Auth -- No --> Denied[403 denied\nNo access mutation]
  Auth -- Yes --> Action{Requested access action}
  Action --> Onboard[(Create invitation or\nexisting-identity link request)]
  Onboard --> Verify[Target user verifies signed SAP identity]
  Verify --> Approval[Confirm or approve provisioning\nas the requested role requires]
  Action --> ProviderChange[Change role, reactivate or revoke]
  Action --> Suspend[Suspend local access]

  Approval --> Rules{Role, identity, version and\nfinal-admin safeguards pass?}
  ProviderChange --> Rules
  Suspend --> Rules
  Rules -- No --> Rejected[400/409 safe response\nAppend rejection audit when applicable]

  Rules -- Yes --> Kind{Provider-backed action?}
  Kind -- No: suspend --> Local[(Deactivate local user\nRevoke active sessions\nState = SUSPENDED)]
  Local --> LocalAudit[Append access audit\nand eligible delivery]

  Kind -- Yes --> Request[(Persist versioned request\nand UserAccessOperation\nKeep access fail-closed)]
  Request --> Broker[Broker performs allowlisted\nread-before / write / read-after]
  Broker --> Proof{Exact immutable identity and\nRole Collection readback?}
  Proof -- No --> Failed[(Keep user inactive or suspended\nStore sanitized failure or reconcile state)]
  Proof -- Yes --> Applied[(Atomically apply local role, capability\nand ACTIVE or REVOKED state)]
  Failed --> Audit[Append immutable access audit]
  Applied --> Audit
  LocalAudit --> Result([Return sanitized administration result])
  Audit --> Delivery[Create eligible inbox/email record\nafter verified outcome]
  Delivery --> Result

